WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.240
Now you understand the problem: everyone is dying while you build missiles.

2
00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:12.940
Time to learn how to fix it. Your solution has three parts: A one percent treaty (stealing money from the murder budget).

3
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:18.660
A one percent Treaty Fund with algorithmic governance (so no one can steal it back).

4
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:26.840
A decentralized framework for drug assessment (making medicine forty-four point one times cheaper).

5
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:35.900
Take money from death, give it to life. The tricky part is convincing humans, who historically prefer the death option.

6
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:47.020
A one percent Treaty. Here's how you redirect twenty-seven point two billion dollars per year from bombs to medicine: You

7
00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:51.380
ask every nation on Earth to cut military spending by one percent.

8
00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:59.940
Just one percent. They keep the other ninety-nine percent for wars and parades and whatever else militaries do when they're

9
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:05.120
not accidentally losing trillions. One percent is a rounding error.

10
00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:10.940
It's what the Pentagon loses between couch cushions. Everyone cuts simultaneously.

11
00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:18.520
Nobody loses "relative power," which is the thing military people care about when they're not busy caring about flags and

12
00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:24.760
saluting. I asked a general if losing one percent of weapons would weaken national security.

13
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:32.240
He said yes. I asked if having one percent fewer weapons pointed at you by every enemy would make you safer.

14
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:42.500
He stopped talking to me. The math is simple: If everyone has one percent fewer weapons, the balance stays exactly the same,

15
00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:53.860
except now there are one percent fewer weapons total. What You Buy With one percent Less War Twenty-seven point two billion

16
00:01:53.860 --> 00:02:02.020
dollars funds: Fifty-four thousand pragmatic clinical trials at five hundred thousand dollars each (the cheap way).

17
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.280
Or twenty-seven million patients in trials at one thousand dollars each.

18
00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:15.120
Or five hundred forty new drug approvals (current rate: fifty drugs per year).

19
00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:21.100
Or curing ten to twenty rare diseases completely in Year One.

20
00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:29.140
Or preventing one hundred eighty thousand deaths annually. That money splits three ways.

21
00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:34.300
Eighty percent goes to clinical trials. Ten percent goes to investors.

22
00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:40.880
Ten percent goes to political incentives. The full allocation breakdown explains why each slice exists.

23
00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:48.500
They say you can't put a price on human life. But apparently the price is somewhere south of pet food.

24
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:56.120
That seems like it should be revised upward (or you should admit you value dogs more than humans, which honestly might be

25
00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:05.620
fair). Your Decentralized Institutes of Health. Once your one percent Treaty is ratified, that twenty-seven point two billion

26
00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:14.540
dollars per year flows into a one percent Treaty Fund. It's a treasury with no C.E.O., no board, and no one to corrupt.

27
00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:23.200
Money flows directly to patients and researchers via algorithmic rules, not through any intermediary organization.

28
00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:31.100
The governance protocol is the opposite of the N.I.H. Instead of two hundred people in a building guessing what to fund

29
00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:35.820
and giving grants to their college roommates, smart contracts hold the treasury.

30
00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:43.820
Patients choose which trials to join. Funding flows automatically to researchers based on patient enrollment.

31
00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:52.200
Trials that work get more patients and more funding. Trials that don't work get defunded, which is apparently a concept

32
00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:57.960
so radical it took your species eighty years to consider. Wishocracy.

33
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:04.160
Wishocracy is how you let eight billion people control a budget without everyone killing each other in meetings.

34
00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:09.520
Anyone can propose how to spend the money. The app shows you random pairs of proposals.

35
00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:13.940
You swipe left or right. Everyone's swipes get aggregated using math.

36
00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:18.680
Money flows automatically to top priorities. No committee. No gatekeepers.

37
00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:26.980
Just billions of micro-decisions that add up to what humanity actually wants, not what 200 people in suits think humanity

38
00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:33.460
wants. Your Decentralized Framework for Drug Assessment. The F.D.A.

39
00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:38.350
currently makes drugs forty-four point one times more expensive than necessary.

40
00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:46.440
Your decentralized framework for drug assessment, or D.F.D.A., does three things: Lets anyone run pragmatic clinical trials

41
00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:52.040
(no permission needed). Tracks what actually works (real-world data, not guesses).

42
00:04:52.700 --> 00:05:00.100
Publishes outcome labels (truth about every treatment). Instead of waiting fourteen years from discovery to patient while

43
00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:06.180
you die, you join a trial. It costs nine hundred twenty-nine dollars instead of forty-one thousand dollars.

44
00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:10.740
You report outcomes through your phone. The A.I. analyzes millions of data points.

45
00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:18.680
The framework publishes rankings: "For your condition, this works seventy-three percent of the time, this works forty-five

46
00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:25.660
percent, this does nothing but costs less.". It's like Amazon reviews except for not dying.

47
00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:29.860
Outcome labels replace "ask your doctor" with actual facts.

48
00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:34.700
"Improves memory thirty-five percent. Reduces symptoms sixty percent.

49
00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:40.200
Causes headaches nine percent of the time. Based on fifty thousand real patients like you."

50
00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:46.480
Just truth. No marketing. No forty-page legal documents written by lawyers having seizures.

51
00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:51.880
Researchers set their own price. Patients choose which trials to join.

52
00:05:51.980 --> 00:06:00.140
Money flows automatically. Markets decide, not committees. Sick people, guided by their doctors and data, choose what gets

53
00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:06.020
funded. Not bureaucrats. Not grant writers. Actual humans who need actual cures.

54
00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.960
Who Wins. The solution only works if everyone wins by winning.

55
00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:19.300
Here's who gets what: Defense contractors keep ninety-nine percent of their budget and get two hundred seventy-two percent

56
00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:25.160
returns on bonds. Pharmaceutical companies get patients to pay them instead of vice versa.

57
00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:29.300
Politicians get campaign donations and avoid losing elections.

58
00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:36.560
Insurance companies want you either dead or immortal, anything but expensively lingering, and cures help.

59
00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:42.520
Billionaires get two hundred seventy-two percent returns, legacy, and naming rights.

60
00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:47.910
Regular people get subsidized treatment, direct democracy, and not dying.

61
00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:53.500
Notice that everyone's selfish reason for participating happens to save humanity.

62
00:06:54.220 --> 00:07:02.080
The system doesn't require anyone to stop being selfish. It just redirects selfishness toward curing diseases instead of

63
00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.980
building bombs. It's like installing a fire alarm that also makes coffee.

64
00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:09.360
You're going to use it even if you don't care about fire safety.

65
00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:15.900
The Scaling Engine. The goal isn't one percent. The goal is one hundred percent.

66
00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:19.640
The one percent treaty is just the door, not the destination.

67
00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:27.520
The ten percent going to Incentive Alignment Bonds creates a perpetual political machine that pushes for expansion.

68
00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:36.780
When one percent passes, two point seven two billion dollars per year flows to people whose entire financial interest is

69
00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:41.880
getting the treaty to two percent. When two percent passes, the pressure doubles.

70
00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.700
The political pressure for expansion *accelerates* with each success.

71
00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:53.620
This creates a ratchet that can eventually redirect all military spending from war to health.

72
00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:59.660
VICTORY Incentive Alignment Bonds are the specific instrument.

73
00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:08.760
They align investors (ten percent returns), politicians (ten percent career incentives), and patients (eighty percent cures)

74
00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:16.660
with the same outcome. The War on Disease. You're declaring war on disease.

75
00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:25.590
But unlike previous wars on abstract concepts (drugs, terror, poverty, Christmas), this one will actually work.

76
00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:34.320
You're using markets instead of bureaucracy. Previous wars built bureaucracies that needed the problem to exist to justify

77
00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:40.120
their existence. This war creates a market that profits from solving the problem.

78
00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:46.740
The difference is like hiring a plumber who gets paid by the hour versus one who gets paid when your toilet works.

79
00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:53.500
One of them is going to take a lot longer. And the benefits cascade beyond medicine.

80
00:08:54.260 --> 00:09:01.760
Addiction, poverty, radicalization, crime; they're all biology problems wearing social-problem costumes.

81
00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:10.700
Fix the biology, and the society fixes itself. It turns out people are much less interested in joining extremist groups

82
00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:17.390
when their brain chemistry works properly. Why This Isn't Clinically Insane.

83
00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:22.880
Post-World War Two: Cut military thirty percent, greatest boom ever.

84
00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:28.740
Post-Cold War: Cut military three percent, nineteen nineties prosperity.

85
00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:35.360
Switzerland: zero point seven percent military budget, richest country in Europe.

86
00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:43.620
You're only asking for one percent. The Meta-Solution. This solution isn't just about ending disease.

87
00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:49.780
It proves that paying people for results works better than paying people for promising results.

88
00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:56.380
You can cure diseases by redirecting one percent of military spending through market mechanisms.

89
00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:04.820
That same template solves education, housing, climate change, and literally any problem your governments currently solve

90
00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:10.740
by forming a committee to discuss forming a committee. The War on Disease is proof of concept.

91
00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:15.620
Victory here means you can fix everything else using the same playbook.

92
00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:20.420
They say if something seems too good to be true, it probably is.

93
00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:28.200
But sometimes things are exactly as good as they seem, and the only reason nobody did them is that everyone was too busy

94
00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:37.040
writing grant proposals about doing them. What Comes Next. The rest of Part Two explains each component in detail: Your

95
00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:41.420
one percent Treaty: How to structure it so countries actually sign it.

96
00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:46.980
Your Decentralized Institutes of Health: How algorithmic governance prevents corruption.

97
00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:53.460
Wishocracy: How to let billions of people control a budget without lobbyists stealing it.

98
00:10:54.080 --> 00:11:02.260
Your decentralized F.D.A., or D.F.D.A.: How to achieve forty-four point one times cost reduction in drug trials.

99
00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:08.120
Aligning Incentives: How to make selfishness save humanity.

100
00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:16.780
Incentive Alignment Bonds: How everyone makes money. The Peace Dividend: Why curing disease accidentally solves everything

101
00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:25.220
else. That's it. That's the plan. If that seems anticlimactic, remember: Every revolution starts with someone doing something

102
00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:33.860
slightly less stupid than what everyone else is doing. In this case, the slightly less stupid thing is redirecting one percent

103
00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:41.240
of the murder budget to the not-dying budget. History will judge whether this was genius or obvious.

104
00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:45.460
But either way, you'll be alive to see it. That's more than you can say for the alternative.
